$ =========================================================================
$ val_vlm_anhedral.bdf — VLM validation case: rectangular wing, AR = 8, -10 deg anhedral
$
$ STEP 58 (V-C-DIH) test deck — out-of-plane (z != 0) lifting surface, MIRROR
$ of val_vlm_dihedral.bdf with the tips canted DOWN (Gamma = -10 deg).
$   Starboard tip LE lowered to (0, 4cosG, -4sinG); port tip to (0,-4cosG,-4sinG).
$
$   Gamma = -10 deg:  cos|G| = 0.98480775,  sin|G| = 0.17364818
$   Semi-span ALONG the canted surface = 4.0 (panel area S = 8.0 unchanged).
$
$ EXPECTED (signed Gamma in the n = (0, -sinG, cosG) formula):
$   Right-wing box normal  n = (0, +sin|G|, cos|G|); left wing (0, -sin|G|, cos|G|).
$   Per box  Fy/Fz = -tan(G) = +tan|G| (starboard) — sign reversed vs dihedral.
$   Side force Fy cancels over the full-span symmetric build (sum ~ 0).
$   Vertical lift identical in magnitude to the +10deg dihedral deck (cos is even).
$
$ Coordinate system: X = freestream, Y = starboard, Z = up.  SYMXZ = 0.
$ Pure rigid VLM — NO structural model, NO splines.
$ =========================================================================
$
SOL 101
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = Rectangular AR=8 wing, -10deg anhedral — rigid VLM
$
